            <ArticleTitle>Occult wrist pain due to capitate nonunion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>402-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Capitate nonunion is an uncommon cause of occult wrist pain. History of wrist injury, tenderness in the distal carpal row, capitate-view x-rays, and special radiographic studies such as bone scan, CT scan, or magnetic resonance imaging can confirm the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
